==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|wonderfully}}, {{m|enm|wunderfullie}}, {{m|enm|wonderfulliche}}, equivalent to {{suf|en|wonderful|ly|id2=adverbial}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-wonderfully.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{IPA|en|/wʌn.də(ɹ).fli/}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a [[wonderful]] manner.
#: {{ux|en|He entertained us '''wonderfully'''.}}
#* '''1992''', Casella and George, ''Explaining the Gibbs Sampler'', in: The American Statistician 46(3) 167&ndash;174
#*: {{quote|en|By freeing statisticians from dealing with complicated calculations, the statistical aspects of a problem can become the main focus. This point is '''wonderfully''' illustrated by Smith and Gelfand (1992).}}
# To an extent inspiring wonder.
#: {{ux|en|His costume was '''wonderfully''' intricate.}}

